// Test: bugfixes/syn002_top_level_generic_type_block_rejected
// Grammar: type_apply_block (list_type)
// Semantic: SYN002 — an apply block (`list<string>:`) is a statement; at file top level it is rejected with a message saying where it belongs (semantic-rules.md §SYN002)
// Fixed in: compiler 0.33.184
// Expected output:
// Expected error:
//   SYN002
//   A type block like `list<string>:` must be inside `start:`, `state:` or a function body
//
// Regression: reported as SYN001 "Unexpected identifier at top level: \"list\"".

list<string>:
	names = []

start:
	print("test")
